# SPARK ERP Frontend Project Structure

## Core Architecture
This is a React 19 + TypeScript ERP frontend application using feature-based architecture. The main entry point is [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx) which loads the routing configuration from [src/routes/index.tsx](mdc:src/routes/index.tsx).

## Key Directories
- **`src/features/`** - Feature-based modules (master-data, stock-opname, authentication, etc.)
- **`src/components/`** - Shared/reusable components organized by type
- **`src/hooks/`** - Custom React hooks including [useDebounceCallback.tsx](mdc:src/hooks/useDebounceCallback.tsx)
- **`src/libs/`** - Library configurations including [axios.ts](mdc:src/libs/axios.ts) and [react-query.tsx](mdc:src/libs/react-query.tsx)
- **`src/store/`** - Zustand state management stores
- **`src/routes/`** - React Router configuration files

## Feature Module Pattern
Each feature follows this structure:
```
features/[feature-name]/
├── components/     # Feature-specific components
├── hooks/         # Feature-specific hooks (useGet, useMutate)
├── types.ts       # TypeScript type definitions
└── page-[feature].tsx  # Main feature page
```

## State Management
- **Zustand** for client state (see [src/store/user.ts](mdc:src/store/user.ts))
- **React Query (TanStack Query)** for server state management
- **React Hook Form** for form state with Zod validation

## UI Framework
- **Mantine UI 8** as the primary component library
- **Emotion** for CSS-in-JS styling
- **PostCSS** for CSS processing with Mantine presets
